From 5799e7f3b7db98074d447ac3121b964cf6445d2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Feder <noreply@splitmind.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:25:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mcp-oauth): budget anonymous writes to OAUTH_KV per UTC
 day

Three unauthenticated requests write to OAUTH_KV, and Workers Free allows
1,000 KV writes a day: POST /oauth/mcp/register, GET /oauth/mcp/authorize
(a consent transaction, reachable with an attacker-hosted CIMD client that
needs no registration), and POST /oauth/mcp/token with a client_assertion (a
replay marker). Using the day's writes up stops token refresh for connected
clients.

When a Durable Object namespace is bound as MCP_OAUTH_ANONYMOUS_WRITES
(class McpOAuthAnonymousWriteBudget, SQLite-backed), registrations and
authorize GETs take a slot from one budget: at most
OOMOL_CONNECT_MCP_OAUTH_MAX_ANONYMOUS_WRITES_PER_DAY (default 100) in total
and ..._PER_IP_PER_DAY (default 20) per CF-Connecting-IP (IPv6 per /64), per
UTC day, both checked and taken in one call under blockConcurrencyWhile.
Registration takes its slot after the redirect allowlist passes. The
authorize slot is taken after the library has validated the client and
redirect URI (parseAuthRequest, describeConsent and the allowlist) and before
beginConsent, which does the KV write, so only requests that would write
use a slot. Over the budget, registration answers invalid_client_metadata
and authorize answers 429 HTML, with no KV write. If the budget errors, or
the per-request env scope is missing, the request is refused. Token requests
carrying client_assertion or client_assertion_type get 401 invalid_client,
read from a clone of the request. Without the binding, behaviour is
unchanged. Consent POSTs, token exchange and refresh never touch the
budget.

The wrapper's own 400 and 401 token responses carry the library's CORS
headers. The bounded token body is parsed with formData(), as the library
does. IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses (::ffff:a.b.c.d) share the IPv4 key.
